{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>נבל תבל</b> — a term of confusion, as in 'ונבלה שפתם'. In this matter you and they will be confounded — this one cries out 'hear me, my lord,' and that one likewise. And you do not know whom to answer, for you do not understand what they are saying, nor do they understand what you are saying." "<b>גם אתה.</b> Rashi explained: to include Aaron, Hur, and the seventy elders. And if you ask: but in the pericope of תשא, at 'ויבן מזבח לפניו,' Rashi explained that Hur saw the altar that they built for the calf — now Hur was killed by them, and this happened on the seventeenth of Tammuz; whereas this pericope was said only after Yom HaKippurim that followed it, as Rashi explained here [that Yitro came after the giving of the Torah]. One may answer: this is what it says: 'נבל תבל גם אתה' — to include Aaron, Hur, and the seventy elders, meaning: even if Hur were standing with you, and with Aaron, and with the seventy elders, you would not be able to suffice for this matter. A parallel to this is what HaShem said to Jeremiah the prophet: 'If Moses and Samuel were to stand before Me' etc. — and they had already departed [from the world]; so too here, Hur had already departed — even so, He mentioned him. But further on [v. 21] He did not mention him, at 'כל העם הזה,' where Rashi explained: Aaron, Nadav, Avihu, and seventy elders of Israel are those who join you now — [this one's] <b>גם העם הזה</b> [means]: that they cannot bear the burden of standing all day to wait for their judgment."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:39.001890268Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}